6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59296</s:story_id></item><item><title>No. 22 West Virginia Welcomes No. 23 Penn State Thursday</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/19/womens-soccer-no-22-west-virginia-welcomes-no-23-penn-state-thursday</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/19/womens-soccer-no-22-west-virginia-welcomes-no-23-penn-state-thursday</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Alexis Pashales of the WVU women's soccer team battles for a ball against a Dayton defender during a match on Aug. 13 in Morgantown." src="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/8/19/TT-WSOC-WVUvsDayton-13__1_.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. (Aug. 19, 2026) – The No. 22-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team continues its season-opening homestand when it welcomes No. 23 Penn State to Morgantown on Thursday, Aug. 20. Kickoff at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium is set for 7 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/19/TT-WSOC-WVUvsDayton-13__1_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/19/TT-WSOC-WVUvsDayton-13__1_.jpg"><media:title>Alexis Pashales of the WVU women's soccer team battles for a ball against a Dayton defender during a match on Aug. 13 in Morgantown.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/19/TT-WSOC-WVUvsDayton-13__1_.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:22:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59295</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU and Mountain State Hoop Legend Willie Akers Passes Away</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/18/mens-basketball-wvu-and-mountain-state-hoop-legend-willie-akers-passes-away</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/18/mens-basketball-wvu-and-mountain-state-hoop-legend-willie-akers-passes-away</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Team captain Willie Akers leads the Mountaineer basketball team out for pregame warmups during a college basketball game at the old Field House in 1960." src="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/8/19/Willie-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Willie Akers, a starting forward on West Virginia University's 1959 NCAA runner-up team, died earlier today in Logan, West Virginia, following months of declining health, according to his son Darren.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/19/Willie-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/19/Willie-Main.jpg"><media:title>Team captain Willie Akers leads the Mountaineer basketball team out for pregame warmups during a college basketball game at the old Field House in 1960.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/19/Willie-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:01:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59294</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineer Athletics Plays Host to Sixth Annual Youth Sports Day</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/18/football-mountaineer-athletics-plays-host-to-sixth-annual-youth-sports-day</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/18/football-mountaineer-athletics-plays-host-to-sixth-annual-youth-sports-day</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="26YouthSportsDay" src="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/8/18/Youth_Sports_Day_1920x1080.png" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Get Moving! WV and Raising Cane's are teaming up with West Virginia University Athletics as hosts of the sixth annual Youth Sports Day on Saturday, Sept. 5, as the Mountaineers take on Coastal Carolina at Milan Puskar Stadium. Get Moving! WV is a local nonprofit dedicated to helping West Virginia's youth live healthy, active lives through community events, nutrition education and programs such as its annual Day of Play.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/18/Youth_Sports_Day_1920x1080.png" /><media:content url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/18/Youth_Sports_Day_1920x1080.png"><media:title>26YouthSportsDay</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/18/Youth_Sports_Day_1920x1080.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:33:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59293</s:story_id></item><item><title>Hard-Working Cook Eying Season Opener Against Coastal Carolina</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/17/football-hard-working-cook-eying-season-opener-against-coastal-carolina</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/17/football-hard-working-cook-eying-season-opener-against-coastal-carolina</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia's Cam Cook runs the football during a preseason practice on the Steve Antoline Family Practice Field in Morgantown, West Virginia." src="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/8/17/Cook-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Rich Rodriguez thought he was getting a good football player when he pursued running back Cam Cook in the transfer portal last winter, and now that he's been here for eight months, he is realizing that he's getting a lot more than just a good football player.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/17/Cook-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/17/Cook-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia's Cam Cook runs the football during a preseason practice on the Steve Antoline Family Practice Field in Morgantown, West Virginia.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/17/Cook-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 15:32:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59292</s:story_id></item><item><title>Pat White Throwback Jersey - Now Available</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/15/football-pat-white-throwback-jersey-now-available</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/8/15/football-pat-white-throwback-jersey-now-available</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Pat White Throwback Jersey is on sale now at the NIL Store" src="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/8/15/FB2026_PatWhiteJerseyCollection_Email.png" /><br /><br />]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/15/FB2026_PatWhiteJerseyCollection_Email.png" /><media:content url="https://admin.wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_